            "heading": "Is Embedded Systems",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "One career-data site splits a typical week as roughly 35% firmware development, 25% debugging and bring-up, 20% RTOS and drivers and 20% testing and documentation (OwnYourCareer, India 2026; it names no dataset, so read it as a sketch)."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "C and C++ for a microcontroller: drivers for sensors, timers, interrupts, communication stacks, and the code that decides what the device does."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A new board arrives and does not boot."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "work",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 1
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:11",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Proof That a Hardware Recruiter Can Check",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Show work early on one platform."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Pass the three proofs with one board project before you call yourself job-ready."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "One board project with code, a photo and a captured signal showing it works."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "proof",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 11
